vidence":"FY2025 net income of 3.751B is about 1.39x operating income of 2.694B. FY2023 net income of 3.136B is about 1.51x operating income of 2.073B. This implies sizable non-operating or one-off items (for example gains, tax effects or other income), but the documents do not break them down. Net income also swung from -0.726B (2022) to +3.136B (2023).","source":"MARKET DATA history"},{"flag":"High leverage","evidence":"Total debt of 42.83B against cash of 1.72B and a market cap of 22.61B. Debt/Equity is 2.327. Debt is roughly 1.9x market cap.","source":"MARKET DATA"},{"flag":"Minor valuation-metric inconsistency","evidence":"Trailing P/E of 7.05 implies EPS of about 20.41 at a price of 143.85. FY2025 net income divided by the share count (3.751B / 157.18M shares) is about 23.86, which implies a P/E of about 6.0. The difference may come from timing or share-count definitions, which the documents do not explain. The Yahoo quote (143.91) also differs slightly from the MARKET DATA price (143.85), probably because of intraday timing.","source":"MARKET DATA; Yahoo Finance - Analysis"}],"data_gaps":["No business description, fleet, customer or strategy information in the documents; the only classification is Industrials / Rental & Leasing Services.","No management or analyst growth estimates (the Yahoo Finance - Analysis Growth Estimates table is empty).","No risk-factor disclosures (stated_risks is empty because nothing was provided).","No filings, footnotes or income statement breakdown, so the drivers of net income exceeding operating income (non-operating items, gains, taxes) are unknown.","No split of capex into growth versus maintenance, and no information on depreciation, asset sales or lease terms.","No debt maturity schedule, interest cost, covenant or liquidity detail.","No quarterly data, guidance, buyback or dividend information.","The unit and basis of the Debt/Equity figure (ratio versus percent) are not specified."]}
Qualitative analysis: {"moat":{"rating":"narrow","sources_of_moat":["Scale: AerCap calls itself the industry leader across aviation leasing, with about 3,500 aircraft, engines and helicopters owned, on order or managed at 12/31/2025","Manufacturer purchasing power: large orders get favorable pricing and delivery terms, and AerCap can secure scarce delivery slots (for example 15 Boeing 787s for 2030-2033, as the world's largest 787 owner)","Funding advantage: investment-grade unsecured debt access at attractive spreads, with an average cost of debt of 4.2%","Platform and remarketing capability: 705 transactions in 2025, an 85% passenger lease extension rate in Q2 2026, and 99% owned-aircraft utilization in 2024","M&A integration track record (ILFC, GECAS), which AerCap itself describes as a key competitive advantage"],"evidence":"The moat comes from scale, cost of funds and OEM relationships. It is not a pricing-power or switching-cost moat. Management says AerCap competes on execution certainty rather than the cheapest lease rate. Q2 2026 showed lease yield up 30bp and net spread up 50bp year over year, and asset sales at a 20% gain margin. Part of this reflects an industry-wide aircraft supply shortage, not only AerCap-specific strengths. AerCap said it can buy narrowbody delivery slots at a price 16-17% below competitors. I rate the moat narrow because aircraft are a cyclical, capital-intensive asset class and competition is still high. Returns depend on the cycle and on airline credit quality. The FY2023-25 FCF figures are negative on a reported basis, because growth capex exceeded operating cash flow. I did not verify the maintenance versus growth capex split.","sources":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000162828026007513/aer-20251231.htm","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-n-v-q2-174137648.html","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/AER/pressreleases/3623571/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://umbrex.com/resources/company-profiles/aercap-holdings-n-v/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000137878925000007/aer-20241231.htm"]},"management":{"rating":"strong","capital_allocation":"Capital allocation has been shareholder-friendly. Since 2023 AerCap has repurchased over 93 million shares, about 40% of those outstanding, for roughly $8B. It returned more than $1.4-1.5B to shareholders in H1 2026 and approved a new $1B buyback on Sep 16, 2026, running to June 2027. It raised the quarterly dividend from $0.27 to $0.40. Leverage is 2.05x, below the 2.5x target, and liquidity is about $22B. Management argues that buybacks beat sale-leasebacks at current economics. In Q2 2026 it raised 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to about $16.80. About $2.80 of that comes from asset-sale gains, and core EPS is about $14.00. Adjusted ROE was 18%. Asset sales for 2026 are expected at $4-5B. One caution: earnings are partly driven by gains on sale, which are cyclical and not guaranteed to recur. Management also chose not to guide to any second-half gains. Aengus Kelly has been CEO since 2011 and has led the ILFC and GECAS deals. The Russia insurance recovery effort has been successful: about $2.5B of pretax recoveries are expected against the $2.7B pretax net charge taken in 2022.","governance_concerns":["Key-person risk: Aengus Kelly has been CEO since 2011. I found no disclosed CEO succession plan in these results, so that is unknown.","Russia: the recovery of stranded aircraft is ongoing. AerCap has litigation against Russian operator insurers and reinsurers. Appeal risk remains (Fidelis said it was considering one), and the size and timing of further recoveries are uncertain.","Legacy contingent litigation: a long-running Brazilian VASP case. AerCap believes it is unlikely to pay damages.","Shareholder engagement in 2026 focused on board composition and executive compensation. The board kept separate CEO and chair roles and is majority independent. I found no specific governance scandal in the sources.","Pay details: I found no data on CEO pay levels or pay-for-performance in the search results, so that is unknown."],"sources":["https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/03/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-090024520.html","https://www.marketscreener.com/news/aercap-approves-1-billion-share-repurchase-program-through-june-2027-ce785bd2dc81ff26","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000095015726000221/ex99-2.htm","https://beinsure.com/news/uk-court-awards-aercap-1bn/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026050456/aer-20260630_d2.htm","https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/stock-buyback-program-declared-by-aercap-nyseaer-board-of-directors-2026-04-29/"]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Near-term outlook is favorable. Management describes demand above supply, with constrained aircraft and engine availability. Lease extension rates were 85-87% in 2026, and secondary-market buyer demand is strong. About half of the less favorable pandemic-era leases have already rolled off. The rest are expected to roll off over the next five years and lift portfolio yields. Risks include higher oil prices and geopolitical shocks that squeeze airline margins, and some weakness in the Middle East and Asia Pacific. If OEM production recovers, the supply shortage that currently supports lease rates and asset values could ease. Long-term growth in air traffic is a general tailwind, but I did not find a quantified industry growth rate, so that is unknown.","competitive_intensity":"Moderate to high overall, but the top end of the market is concentrated and benefiting from the supply shortage. The 20-F says the business is highly competitive. Competitors include manufacturers, financial institutions, other lessors, brokers and airlines. Competition is based on delivery dates, lease rates, terms and aircraft condition. Scale and cost of funds give large lessors an edge over smaller ones.","key_competitors":["SMBC Aviation Capital","Air Lease Corporation","Avolon","BOC Aviation","Dubai Aerospace Enterprise (DAE)","Aviation Capital Group","Aircraft manufacturers, banks and other financial institutions, and airlines (per the 20-F)"]},"catalysts":["H2 2026 asset sales, guided at $4-5B for the full year, and gain-on-sale margins","Continued buybacks: $1B program through June 2027, and 2026 EPS guidance of about $16.80","Leverage of 2.05x is below the 2.5x target, which leaves room for buybacks or growth investment","Continued roll-off of less favorable pandemic-era leases, which should lift lease yields over the next five years","Further Russia-related insurance recoveries from litigation against operator insurers and reinsurers","Deliveries of the 787 order and other widebody positions, which tighten supply and support lease rates","Risks to watch: higher oil prices and geopolitical shocks that could hurt airline credit, and an easing of the supply shortage"],"citations":["https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/aercap-q2-earnings-call-highlights-2026-07-29/","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-090024520.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-n-v-q2-174137648.html","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/AER/pressreleases/3623571/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/03/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://ca.investing.com/news/company-news/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-highlights-record-asset-sales-raised--4762618","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026028212/aercap2026firstquarterearn.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000162828026007513/aer-20251231.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000137878925000007/aer-20241231.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000104746918001434/a2234723z20-f.htm","https://umbrex.com/resources/company-profiles/aercap-holdings-n-v/","https://www.marketscreener.com/news/aercap-approves-1-billion-share-repurchase-program-through-june-2027-ce785bd2dc81ff26","https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/stock-buyback-program-declared-by-aercap-nyseaer-board-of-directors-2026-04-29/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000095015726000221/ex99-2.htm","https://beinsure.com/news/uk-court-awards-aercap-1bn/","https://www.hsfkramer.com/notes/insurance/2025-posts/russian-aircraft-policy-claims-update-on-appeal-and-costs","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026050456/aer-20260630_d2.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026028212/aer-03312026xinterimreport.htm"]}
