anscript/","https://umbrex.com/resources/company-profiles/aercap-holdings-n-v/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000137878925000007/aer-20241231.htm"]},"management":{"rating":"strong","capital_allocation":"Capital allocation has been shareholder-friendly. Since 2023 AerCap has repurchased over 93 million shares, about 40% of those outstanding, for roughly $8B. It returned more than $1.4-1.5B to shareholders in H1 2026 and approved a new $1B buyback on Sep 16, 2026, running to June 2027. It raised the quarterly dividend from $0.27 to $0.40. Leverage is 2.05x, below the 2.5x target, and liquidity is about $22B. Management argues that buybacks beat sale-leasebacks at current economics. In Q2 2026 it raised 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to about $16.80. About $2.80 of that comes from asset-sale gains, and core EPS is about $14.00. Adjusted ROE was 18%. Asset sales for 2026 are expected at $4-5B. One caution: earnings are partly driven by gains on sale, which are cyclical and not guaranteed to recur. Management also chose not to guide to any second-half gains. Aengus Kelly has been CEO since 2011 and has led the ILFC and GECAS deals. The Russia insurance recovery effort has been successful: about $2.5B of pretax recoveries are expected against the $2.7B pretax net charge taken in 2022.","governance_concerns":["Key-person risk: Aengus Kelly has been CEO since 2011. I found no disclosed CEO succession plan in these results, so that is unknown.","Russia: the recovery of stranded aircraft is ongoing. AerCap has litigation against Russian operator insurers and reinsurers. Appeal risk remains (Fidelis said it was considering one), and the size and timing of further recoveries are uncertain.","Legacy contingent litigation: a long-running Brazilian VASP case. AerCap believes it is unlikely to pay damages.","Shareholder engagement in 2026 focused on board composition and executive compensation. The board kept separate CEO and chair roles and is majority independent. I found no specific governance scandal in the sources.","Pay details: I found no data on CEO pay levels or pay-for-performance in the search results, so that is unknown."],"sources":["https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/03/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-090024520.html","https://www.marketscreener.com/news/aercap-approves-1-billion-share-repurchase-program-through-june-2027-ce785bd2dc81ff26","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000095015726000221/ex99-2.htm","https://beinsure.com/news/uk-court-awards-aercap-1bn/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026050456/aer-20260630_d2.htm","https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/stock-buyback-program-declared-by-aercap-nyseaer-board-of-directors-2026-04-29/"]},"industry":{"growth_outlook":"Near-term outlook is favorable. Management describes demand above supply, with constrained aircraft and engine availability. Lease extension rates were 85-87% in 2026, and secondary-market buyer demand is strong. About half of the less favorable pandemic-era leases have already rolled off. The rest are expected to roll off over the next five years and lift portfolio yields. Risks include higher oil prices and geopolitical shocks that squeeze airline margins, and some weakness in the Middle East and Asia Pacific. If OEM production recovers, the supply shortage that currently supports lease rates and asset values could ease. Long-term growth in air traffic is a general tailwind, but I did not find a quantified industry growth rate, so that is unknown.","competitive_intensity":"Moderate to high overall, but the top end of the market is concentrated and benefiting from the supply shortage. The 20-F says the business is highly competitive. Competitors include manufacturers, financial institutions, other lessors, brokers and airlines. Competition is based on delivery dates, lease rates, terms and aircraft condition. Scale and cost of funds give large lessors an edge over smaller ones.","key_competitors":["SMBC Aviation Capital","Air Lease Corporation","Avolon","BOC Aviation","Dubai Aerospace Enterprise (DAE)","Aviation Capital Group","Aircraft manufacturers, banks and other financial institutions, and airlines (per the 20-F)"]},"catalysts":["H2 2026 asset sales, guided at $4-5B for the full year, and gain-on-sale margins","Continued buybacks: $1B program through June 2027, and 2026 EPS guidance of about $16.80","Leverage of 2.05x is below the 2.5x target, which leaves room for buybacks or growth investment","Continued roll-off of less favorable pandemic-era leases, which should lift lease yields over the next five years","Further Russia-related insurance recoveries from litigation against operator insurers and reinsurers","Deliveries of the 787 order and other widebody positions, which tighten supply and support lease rates","Risks to watch: higher oil prices and geopolitical shocks that could hurt airline credit, and an easing of the supply shortage"],"citations":["https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/aercap-q2-earnings-call-highlights-2026-07-29/","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-090024520.html","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aercap-holdings-n-v-q2-174137648.html","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/AER/pressreleases/3623571/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/03/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://ca.investing.com/news/company-news/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-highlights-record-asset-sales-raised--4762618","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026028212/aercap2026firstquarterearn.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000162828026007513/aer-20251231.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000137878925000007/aer-20241231.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000104746918001434/a2234723z20-f.htm","https://umbrex.com/resources/company-profiles/aercap-holdings-n-v/","https://www.marketscreener.com/news/aercap-approves-1-billion-share-repurchase-program-through-june-2027-ce785bd2dc81ff26","https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/stock-buyback-program-declared-by-aercap-nyseaer-board-of-directors-2026-04-29/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000095015726000221/ex99-2.htm","https://beinsure.com/news/uk-court-awards-aercap-1bn/","https://www.hsfkramer.com/notes/insurance/2025-posts/russian-aircraft-policy-claims-update-on-appeal-and-costs","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026050456/aer-20260630_d2.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001378789/000162828026028212/aer-03312026xinterimreport.htm"]}
