## 1. Executive summary

The recommendation comes from a rule engine, and this report explains it without altering it. The label rests on one failed check: **the DCF valuation is not reliable**. Average free cash flow (FCF) over FY2023–FY2025 is negative (about -$944M), so no bear/base/bull fair-value range could be built. (Source: Valuation output.)

- **Headline multiples look cheap but are not clean.** Trailing P/E is 7.05, forward P/E 7.89, P/B 1.207 and ROE 18.66% (MARKET DATA). Trailing earnings include items that are unlikely to repeat. Net income was about 1.39x operating income in FY2025 (Filings analysis).
- **Reported cash generation is weak.** FCF was -$0.971B, -$1.180B and -$0.681B in FY2023–FY2025, cumulatively about -$2.83B. Net income over the same span was about +$8.99B (MARKET DATA history, derived).
- **Leverage is high.** Total debt is $42.83B against $1.72B of cash and a $22.61B market cap (MARKET DATA).
- **The franchise looks solid on qualitative grounds.** The moat is rated narrow and management strong. These ratings come from the Qualitative analysis, citing the [FY2025 20-F](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000162828026007513/aer-20251231.htm) and Q2 2026 earnings materials.
- **The skeptic panel rated the bear case "minor".** It described the issues as valuation and cycle risk, not fraud or an impaired franchise. The AVOID label should therefore be read mainly as "we cannot reliably value this on a cash-flow basis" and not as evidence of business failure.

*Uncertainty:* The business description in the filings extract was nearly empty. Most business and management detail comes from secondary sources and has not been independently verified here.

