## 2. Business overview

- **Classification:** Industrials / Rental & Leasing Services, reporting in USD (MARKET DATA). The filings extract provided no further operating description.
- **Scale (company-reported, via qualitative research):** AerCap describes itself as the industry leader in aviation leasing, with about 3,500 aircraft, engines and helicopters owned, on order or managed at 12/31/2025 ([FY2025 20-F](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1378789/000162828026007513/aer-20251231.htm)). It is also the world's largest 787 owner ([Q2 2026 call transcript](https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/AER/pressreleases/3623571/aercap-aer-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/)).
- **Competitors:** SMBC Aviation Capital, Air Lease Corporation, Avolon, BOC Aviation, Dubai Aerospace Enterprise and Aviation Capital Group. The 20-F also names manufacturers, banks and airlines.
- **Industry backdrop:** Management describes demand above supply, with constrained aircraft and engine availability. Lease extension rates were 85–87% in 2026. Risks include higher oil prices, geopolitical shocks and Middle East and Asia Pacific weakness. A recovery in OEM production could ease the shortage that currently supports lease rates and asset values. No quantified industry growth rate was found.

